## How the list is organised

**Rust has no weapon classes.** The game puts every weapon in one crafting
and inventory category, **Weapons** (Facepunch's wiki lists the same game
categories: Weapons, Construction, Items, Resources, Attire, Tools, Medical,
Food, Ammo, Traps, Components, Electrical, Fun, Misc). So the groups are ours,
named from the words Facepunch's own item descriptions use ("semi automatic
rifle", "machine gun", "Shotgun", "pistol", "grenade launcher", "bow",
"melee weapon", "grenade"), in the order guns, launchers, bows, special,
melee, grenades. The group ids are chosen so the app shows the right class
picture (`marksman_rifles` for the semi-automatic rifles; `lmgs` for the
machine guns).

- **Assault Rifles:** Assault Rifle, LR-300 Assault Rifle.
- **Semi-Automatic Rifles** (id `marksman_rifles`): Semi-Automatic Rifle, M39
  Rifle, SKS (all three described by Facepunch as semi automatic rifles).
- **Sniper Rifles:** Bolt Action Rifle, L96 Rifle (Double Eleven's Dev Blog #7
  calls the L96 "This sniper").
- **SMGs:** Handmade SMG, Custom SMG, Thompson, MP5A4.
- **Machine Guns** (id `lmgs`): M249, HMLMG, Minigun.
- **Shotguns:** Waterpipe, Double Barrel, Pump, Spas-12, M4, Blunderbuss.
- **Pistols:** Eoka Pistol, Nailgun, Revolver, Semi-Automatic Pistol, Python
  Revolver, M92 Pistol, Prototype 17, High Caliber Revolver.
- **Launchers:** Rocket Launcher, Multiple Grenade Launcher, Homing Missile
  Launcher.
- **Bows:** Hunting Bow, Crossbow, Compound Bow.
- **Special:** Flame Thrower, Military Flame Thrower, Speargun (fires only
  underwater), Snowball Gun (Christmas only).
- **Melee:** the melee weapons in Facepunch's Weapons category. Hatchets,
  pickaxes, the Rock, Torch, Salvaged Axe/Icepick/Hammer, Chainsaw and
  Jackhammer hit too, but the game files them under **Tools**, so they are
  left out.
- **Grenades:** F1 Grenade, Beancan Grenade, Molotov Cocktail, Flashbang (all
  in the Weapons category). Satchel Charge, Timed Explosive Charge and Smoke
  Grenade are in **Tools** and left out.

**`fireMode`** is set only where Facepunch's item text or name says it:
"machine rifle"/"machine gun"/"automatic firearm" = `auto`; "semi
automatic"/"Semi-Automatic" = `semi`; Bolt Action = `bolt`; Pump = `pump`;
Prototype 17 "built-in 3 round burst fire mode" = `burst`. The rest (Nailgun,
LR-300, L96,
Waterpipe, Double Barrel, Eoka, Revolver, Python, High Caliber Revolver,
launchers but the MGL, bows) are left unset rather than guessed.

**Rarity: none.** Rust weapons have no rarity tiers or colours, so there is no
`tiers`.

## Console versus PC

Rust on PC (Facepunch) is ahead of the console edition. **In Facepunch's PC
Weapons category but not named on any Double Eleven page, so left out:**
Mini Crossbow, Blow Pipe, Boomerang, Ballista, Mounted Ballista, Catapult,
Battering Ram, Siege Tower, Paintball Gun, Bee Grenade, Vampire Stake, Skinning
Knife, Water Gun and Water Pistol (the console Sunburn Pack sells "water guns",
a toy). PC's "M16A2" has an icon on Facepunch's server (`m16a2_512.png`) but no
item page and no console mention, so it is left out too.

**Kept but marked `uncertain`, because Facepunch lists them and no console
page names them:** Wooden Spear, Machete, Salvaged Sword, Longsword, Mace.
They are long-standing PC melee weapons, so they are probably on console, but
nothing official read here says so. Also uncertain: **M92 Pistol** (Double
Eleven names it only as a Tunnel Dweller's weapon, Dev Blog #54), **Salvaged
Cleaver** (the console note says only "cleaver"), **Blunderbuss** (first
named on console in a 2026-02-26 fix; arrival date unknown) and the event-only
weapons (Snowball Gun, Candy Cane Club, Sickle, Butcher Knife, Pitchfork).

**Skins are not weapons.** "RPG Launcher" ([RPG DLC](https://rust.double11.com/store/rpg-launcher)),
"Space LR-300", "Huntsman Bolt Action Rifle", "Oni Rocket Launcher" and the
like are console store skins of the weapons here, not separate items. PC-only
item variants (Ice, Jungle, Diver and Medieval Assault Rifles) are not in the
console notes and are left out.

## What is not checked

- How the console HUD shows the held weapon (its name or only its icon in the
  belt) is not checked on a real frame; that is the `review` on the catalog.
- The pictures are PC icons, assumed to match the console item art.

